// authenticateUserWithOAuth.php
function authenticateUserWithOAuth($username, $password) {
    // Initialize session and OAuth client instances
    $session = new Session();
    $oauthClient = new OAuthClient();

    try {
        // Authenticate user with provided credentials
        $accessToken = $oauthClient->authenticate($username, $password);

        if (!$accessToken) {
            throw new Exception("Authentication failed");
        }

        // Store the access token securely in session
        $session->set('access_token', $accessToken);

        // Fetch additional user-specific data using the stored access token
        $userData = $oauthClient->getUserData($accessToken);

        if (!$userData) {
            throw new Exception("Error fetching user data");
        }

        return $userData;
    } catch (Exception $e) {
        // Handle and log errors gracefully
        error_log($e->getMessage());
        return false;
    }
}

// resolveHostname.c
#include <arpa/inet.h>
#include <netdb.h>
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

void resolveHostname(const char *hostname, u_char **ipAddress) {
    struct addrinfo hints, *result;
    int status = 0;

    memset(&hints, 0, sizeof(hints));
    hints.ai_family = AF_INET; // IPv4 only for simplicity
    hints.ai_socktype = SOCK_STREAM;

    if (getaddrinfo(hostname, NULL, &hints, &result) != 0) {
        fprintf(stderr, "getaddrinfo: %s\n", gai_strerror(errno));
        *ipAddress = NULL;
        return;
    }

    // Use the first returned address info
    void *addr = result->ai_addr;
    socklen_t addrLen = result->ai_addrlen;
    struct sockaddr_in *sockAddrIn = (struct sockaddr_in *)addr;

    u_char ip[4];
    for (int i = 0; i < 4; ++i) {
        ip[i] = ((u_char *)&sockAddrIn->sin_addr)[i];
    }

    *ipAddress = ip;

    freeaddrinfo(result);
}
```

This code provides two separate files: `authenticateUserWithOAuth.php` and `resolveHostname.c`. The PHP file contains the `authenticateUserWithOAuth()` function, which integrates with an OAuth 2.0 client for user authentication and fetches additional user-specific data. Error handling is implemented using exception handling mechanisms in PHP.

The C file contains the `resolveHostname()` function that performs DNS resolution for a given hostname using standard library functions provided by glibc (getaddrinfo()). It returns an IP address in a u_char array and includes error handling mechanisms to gracefully handle DNS resolution failures.']

