The function uses the `UseRedisConfiguration()` method to integrate with an external configuration management service (assuming Redis in this example). You should replace it with your preferred method for dynamic configuration if needed. It also includes a timeout mechanism by using exception handling and returning null when an error occurs during startup.

To minimize memory usage, I suggest using lazy loading for services when needed, and consider using an in-memory cache (e.g., Redis) to store frequently accessed data instead of reloading it from disk on each request. Lastly, the function can handle dynamic updates to the application configuration without restarting the entire server by reading the configuration from the specified file at each request.']

