['```php
class User {
    private $db;
    private $api;
    private $cache;
    private $log;

    public function __construct(PDO $db, ApiClient $api, Cache $cache, Logger $log) {
        $this->db = $db;
        $this->api = $api;
        $this->cache = $cache;
        $this->log = $log;
    }

    public function updateUserStatus($userId) {
        // Load user session token from cache, or fetch it from the database if not available in cache
        $token = $this->cache->get('user_' . $userId . '_token') ?: $this->db->query("SELECT session_token FROM users WHERE id = ?", [$userId])->fetchColumn();

        try {
            // Validate the user session token using an external API
            if (!$this->api->validateToken($token)) {
                $this->log->error("Invalid token for user #{$userId}", ['token' => $token]);
                throw new \Exception('Invalid token', 401);
            }
        } catch (\Exception $e) {
            $this->log->error("API call failed: {$e->getMessage()}", ['user_id' => $userId, 'error' => $e->getMessage()]);
            throw new \Exception('API call failed', 503);
        }

        // Atomically update the user status, last modified IP address, and last modified date in the database table
        $this->db->beginTransaction();
        try {
            $ipAddress = $_SERVER['REMOTE_ADDR'];
            $currentTime = new DateTime('NOW', new DateTimeZone('UTC'));
            $this->db->exec("UPDATE users SET status = ?, last_modified_ip = ?, last_modified = ? WHERE id = ?", ['active', $ipAddress, $currentTime->format('Y-m-d H:i:s'), $userId]);
            $this->db->commit();
        } catch (\Exception $e) {
            $this->db->rollback();
            throw new \Exception('Database update failed', 500);
        }

        // Store the user session token in cache for future use (with a defined expiration time)
        $this->cache->set('user_' . $userId . '_token', $token, 3600); // Cache expires after 1 hour

        $this->log->info("User #{$userId} status updated successfully", ['ip_address' => $ipAddress]);
        return 'Success';
    }
}
```

In this example, I have created a User class that handles the specified programming task. The `updateUserStatus()` function loads the user session token either from cache or the database, validates it using an external API, and atomically updates the user's status, last modified IP address, and last modified date in the database table.

The code utilizes a caching mechanism to reduce database load and improve performance by storing the user session token for future use (with an expiration time of 1 hour). In case of network failures during API calls, the function catches exceptions and logs the errors accordingly. The solution is designed to scale efficiently as the number of users grows and optimized for low latency under high traffic conditions by using transactions in the database.

For better reusability and modularity, external dependencies such as PDO for database connection, ApiClient for API calls, Cache for caching, and Logger for logging are passed through the constructor of the User class.']

